7. Evaluation, Benchmarking and Deployment
Q54. How would you evaluate a new model-routing strategy?
Answer: Execute existing and candidate routing policies against identical representative datasets and compare task success, cost, latency and safety.
Q55. How would you measure p95 latency?
Answer: Record end-to-end request durations using OpenTelemetry histograms and calculate the 95th-percentile latency across representative workloads.
Q56. How would you measure model-routing effectiveness?
Answer: Track task success, model-selection accuracy, escalation rates, deterministic bypass rates and cost per successful task.
Q57. How would you prevent quality regression during cost optimization?
Answer: Enforce task-specific minimum quality thresholds and maximum permitted regressions through automated evaluation release gates.
Q58. How would you implement routing-policy canary deployment?
Answer: Use tenant-aware feature flags or deployment controllers to expose candidate routing policies to controlled production traffic.
Q59. How would you implement automatic routing rollback?
Answer: Restore the previous routing-policy version when monitored quality, cost, latency or security conditions violate release thresholds.
Q60. How would you implement continuous model-routing optimization?
Answer: Analyze production traces, update model capability benchmarks and evaluate revised routing policies before controlled deployment.
