11. Top 20 Security Concepts to Memorize
Concept
One-line revision answer
Zero Trust
Never implicitly trust a user, agent, service or network location.
Least Privilege
Grant only the permissions necessary to perform an assigned operation.
Least Agency
Grant only the autonomy necessary to accomplish an assigned objective.
Workload Identity
Establish a verifiable identity for each running agent or service.
Delegated Authorization
Allow an agent to act within explicitly delegated user authority.
Effective Permissions
Intersect agent capabilities, user permissions and enterprise policies.
Confused Deputy
A privileged service is manipulated into exercising authority improperly for another party.
PDP
Evaluates whether an operation is authorized.
PEP
Enforces the authorization decision before execution.
RBAC
Controls access through predefined roles.
ABAC
Controls access through identity, resource and contextual attributes.
Fail Closed
Deny protected operations when authorization cannot be verified.
Prompt Injection
Untrusted content attempts to manipulate model behavior.
Indirect Prompt Injection
Malicious instructions arrive through retrieved data or external tool responses.
Data Exfiltration
Unauthorized transmission of protected information.
DLP
Detects and restricts unauthorized movement of sensitive information.
Human-in-the-Loop
Requires authorized human intervention at defined workflow checkpoints.
Separation of Duties
Prevents a single actor from independently authorizing designated sensitive operations.
TOCTOU
A security-relevant condition changes between authorization and execution.
Defense in Depth
Uses multiple independent security controls to contain failures.
